#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073716 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aabbe3f2-c799-5d31-b5c1-8d21b32afccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Division Problem Represented by a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "4fae5cf1-65c9-5217-89ec-54b40e80f293" :question/math-academy-id "e-14418" :question/problem "What division problem is represented by the model below?\n\n![](images/b2/b2e5fb40e703cb3d93f22fd315852930eaab540445e3f570e8de3dacfdc83e0b.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/78/785deacac749a6ed43e5e6a2638677e8ff9e9b58087cb4e471ea85fd50609ce6.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073487 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073717 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91201453-ec4d-55a4-8a7b-eae34fca9f8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Divisor in a Division Model"}] :question/id #uuid "9cd2d717-01de-5319-8759-2990e79d64ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-14420" :question/problem "What number is missing from the division problem below?\n\n![](images/cf/cf2500f82f337e5635a5ca9854579e3b883f42cde4598d4324c94364bf998a0d.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{15}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/ed/ed5517a9242aed1c5b521ca07772dacbb7c96a73c69d4d9c6214a098742358e2.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $5$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $5$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073488 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bb96a84-3329-5702-ae45-a7d0ad2a95c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Result in a Division Model"}] :question/id #uuid "62d9f262-e419-5a9d-a5cb-741c34613570" :question/math-academy-id "e-14423" :question/problem "What picture is missing from the division model below?\n\n![](images/9c/9cc5d672cb3c12ceb7704f5136e9b7ecae61d11a9418acf3b8e1cbb9e8f044f7.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that in the model, we have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to divide by $\\color{blue}3$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/30/30f9bbc604d35a9a15e1418c0cf80eca87fe4d704287c15fb8de7426eb9e3de9.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ of the whole.\n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/95/951a4bc0607c53aa0c5ed9cebe664b630acf226a6f9844fd9d1b8e6ae952d0ed.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073489 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a903aacb-718a-52f6-8be7-a7043358b7bb" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Model to Solve a Division Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "c6e1860a-9fe5-559c-8a19-6ed98335659b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14424" :question/problem "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4.$\n\n![](images/8e/8eccf163bffabb43593188590a1f995544f3d1ac0aebcdd87dce638b230f8165.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a3/a34a3fb198ef2ea79f8baf8f0acbdbdc179c6259c614824315d3d96e5ea4e921.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{1}{16}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073717 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91201453-ec4d-55a4-8a7b-eae34fca9f8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Divisor in a Division Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d8eb349-8d81-5b23-8b12-380de2e96e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d8eb349-8d81-5b23-8b12-380de2e96e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426178} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc9faf43-6aee-5f72-8f40-0ad2d2596130" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c3b94acc-11cb-5adf-8b47-557b2f1acf0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-222989" :question/problem "Insert the missing number in the division problem below.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" height=\"100\" rules=\"all\" width=\"100\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"3\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$÷$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$=$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" height=\"100\" rules=\"all\" width=\"100\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{1}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{1}{35}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/34/3446d5184d3cd128aabaf7f571973e621c1c0c612b01418f1d470bdb616d5ccd.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $7$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $7$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}÷7=\\frac{1}{35}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a903aacb-718a-52f6-8be7-a7043358b7bb" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Model to Solve a Division Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9639c2f8-c551-5518-8e44-6c25f7003f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9639c2f8-c551-5518-8e44-6c25f7003f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426189} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a590395-4bd5-5e91-8534-fa05bc66616f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "082cc509-e07c-556d-9f17-73ffd105d8e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-223013" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d3157d3ef0c1514584b3f624fb1b274be37c2bd92a9c3848f4d75bebe9cb2a7.png)\n\nUse the model above to solve the following division problem.\n\n$\\frac{1}{5}÷7=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to divide by $7$, we split the whole into $7$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/bb/bb8362ba449f1dc6dde21397007739a59cb9f99a240dce42970b6fd29d8d3b19.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{1}{35}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}÷7=\\frac{1}{35}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073716 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aabbe3f2-c799-5d31-b5c1-8d21b32afccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Division Problem Represented by a Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6033979d-fcff-5b80-a44c-74846773a269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}÷3=\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426182} {:answer/id #uuid "82b978b3-88f8-5487-a4c7-aacf15819594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}÷3=\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426186} {:answer/id #uuid "893ca7db-b167-502a-9ff3-5c5129795f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}÷3=\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426188} {:answer/id #uuid "d670e87e-4af8-5017-aca5-9d0544eec322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}÷9=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426199} {:answer/id #uuid "f365f6b0-ab9c-5d4e-93e4-1a8043e3fdc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}÷3=\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f365f6b0-ab9c-5d4e-93e4-1a8043e3fdc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}÷3=\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426204} :answer-field/id #uuid "4350a32a-8d19-53b4-b88e-83081a8487c1" :answer-fie